operator: Hey! So I'm back.
operator: ...
- That was quick!
	operator: I mean, that's what I'm here for.
	operator: You're boots on the ground, I'm eyes in the sky.
	operator: But anyway, I have some strange news.
	- What's up?
		jump cont1
label cont1
operator: So these vines are a kind of strangler fig.
operator: On it's own, that's not such a bad thing, despite the scary name.
operator: A normal strangler fig in its native environment will still kill its host,
operator: But before it does its host in, it can serve as a scaffold that strengthens and supports it.
operator: Heck, they're even known to play host to some rare insect species and the birds that predate on them.
operator: The problem is, someone made these strangler figs particularly aggressive.
operator: They're growing too fast and too large, overtaking too much canopy and sucking up too much of the nitrogen in the soil in the process.
operator: ...
- Someone *made* them?
	operator: That's how it seems to me, yeah.
	operator: Again, not a bad thing on its own.
	operator: You can engineer a plant to fill the gaps in a population's vitamin intake, or to better capture carbon.
	operator: But whoever made these strangler figs made them particularly vigorous, and that's destabilized this forest's ecology.
	operator: So we're gonna need you to figure out who did this and why.
	operator: In other words, our mission has gone from a find-and-preserve to an explore-and-investigate.
	- What does that mean?
		operator: For us? Two things, mostly.
		operator: One\: you've been granted provisional permission to access the Green Arsenal in your investigation.
		operator: I'll lend you my Pea Shooter to use as a focus towards that end.
		operator: Two\: I'm to collect any reports and updates from you as you proceed.
		operator: Basically, you can save the progress of your investigation by reporting to me at any drop-point.
		jump any_questions
label any_questions
operator: Any other questions?
- Green Arsenal?
	operator: When the need arises, Gardeners and Operators like you and me are sometimes given access to a system of burgeoning magic ---
	operator: It accelerates the growth and exaggerates the characteristics of plant types we encounter. We call this system the Green Arsenal.
	operator: A lily pad grows large and strong enough to support a person's weight; a sweet pea or wood sorrel's exploding seed packs a bigger punch; a sacred lotus' heat generation becomes scalding.
	operator: We sometimes have to use these qualities creatively to navigate a forest as heavily impacted as this one.
	jump any_questions
- Pea Shooter?
	operator: My loyal six-shooter. It's been enchanted to have an infinite supply of partridge pea seeds as ammunition,
	operator: But it can also be supplied with any useful seeds you find during your investigation for use with the Green Arsenal.
	operator: Partridge peas are native to the area, and can help replenish the depleted nitrogen in the soil, so don't worry too much about spreading them around.
	jump any_questions
- Drop-point?
	operator: A spot you can call me down like this! You'll know them when you see them.
	jump any_questions
- Not really.
	jump questions_done
label questions_done
operator: Alright, before I send you off, there are a couple more things we should talk about.
operator: Chiefly, the R button on that there Pea Shooter will open up its cylinder and let you reload it with your seeds.
operator: From my observations, when the engineered strangler fig grows as large as it has here, its structure becomes more unstable and therefore more susceptible to collapse.
operator: Look for weak points in its scaffold and give them a few shots with the Pea Shooter to proceed.
operator: By my estimation, there should be about 3 in this area.
operator: And finally, when I talk to you from now on, I'll ask you whether you want to record any progress in your investigation.
operator: Let's practice\:
operator: "Would you like to record any progress in your investigation?"
- Yes
	operator: Saving progress...
	[signal arg="save_signal"]
	operator: Save complete.
	jump save_done
- No
	operator: Roger dodger! I'll be here if you need to save progress in the future.
	jump save_done
label save_done
operator: At that, I wish you the best of luck, Gardener.
operator: See you on the flip side!
[signal arg="scene_end_op"]
[end_timeline]